/T (The objective is to replace correlated original variables with a smaller number of uncorrelated factors. The new variables, or factors, should explain as much of the variation in the original data as possible while preserving its correlation structure. In this study, we will search for a latent political variable - an unobserved variable that is not measured directly but influences the variables being analyzed.)
/E (The objective is to replace correlated original variables with a smaller number of uncorrelated factors. The new variables, or factors, should explain as much of the variation in the original data as possible while preserving its correlation structure. In this study, we will search for a latent political variable - an unobserved variable that is not measured directly but influences the variables being analyzed.)
