/T (Cronbach's alpha indicates that the data are moderately consistent, meaning that factors may exist, although at this stage it is not yet known what they are. The characteristics demonstrate a moderate degree of association. In Bartlett's test, the null hypothesis was rejected, which means that the correlation matrix contains relationships between the characteristics. The KMO coefficient indicates that the relationships are sufficiently strong to conduct factor analysis. The MSA values for each variable are above 0.6, so there is no need to remove any of the variables.)
