/E (In the scree plot above, it can be clearly seen that only two points remain above the green line representing Cattell's criterion. This indicates that the subsequent analysis will be conducted with the assumption that we are looking for two latent variables. If another criterion were applied, for example one allowing factors with eigenvalues greater than 0.7 rather than Cattell's criterion of greater than 1, three factors would be included in the subsequent analysis. This could result in a larger proportion of the variance being explained.)
