/P 226 0 R
/E (When comparing the two factor-analysis methods, it turns out that factor analysis with Varimax rotation is more effective. It identifies the factors more precisely, and a larger number of the variables forming them exceed a loading value of 0.6. Interestingly, as many as two variables have a Hoffman index of 2.0, which indicates that these variables influence Factors 1 and 2 to the same degree. Variables 14 and 15 do not form any latent variable. They could have been removed at an earlier stage of the analysis or retained as a separate set, as shown in the Spearman correlation matrix.)
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [7]
>>
