/P 228 0 R
/E (MASS - refers to the weight or importance assigned to individual rows and columns of a contingency table. Masses reflect the proportional contribution of each row and column to the total number of observations, helping to understand their relative importance in the analysis.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
914 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 228 0 R
/E (INERTIA - a measure of the total variance in the data that describes the distribution of points in multidimensional space. It is used to assess the quality of representing the data using a specific number of dimensions. Higher inertia values indicate that a given dimension explains a larger proportion of the total variance.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
915 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
