/Title (Correspondence analysis is an exploratory statistical method used to examine the co-occurrence of categories of nominal variables. Its main purpose is to provide a graphical representation of relationships and associations between categories of two or more qualitative variables. This makes it easier to interpret the data and identify underlying structures. The technique allows nominal data to be presented using one-, two-, or three-dimensional plots, which are used to visualize relationships between the categories of the variables being analyzed.)
